   "isSolo": true,
   "levelText": "Mythic",
   "page": 0,
   "description": "<p><em>Gargantuan dragon (metallic)</em></p><p><strong>GM:</strong> The Platinum Dragonlord, also Xymor or Marduk, king of the good dragons and, with Tiamat, father of Tiahane. His Deteron paladin orders and the rites of Komodo Isle keep his name. He champions war against the giants and, in matters of law, defers to Torm. He walks among mortals in disguise and judges them by how they treat a frail old man.</p><p><strong>Solo:</strong> acts twice a round, on its initiative and again 10 lower (the system adds its second turn; the second repeats its attacks, never a spell or limited ability). Anything that stops it acting, attacking, moving or casting ends after two of its turns (one, the second time in a fight), then nothing of the kind affects it until the end of the following round; the first time it drops to half HP every condition and hostile effect ends and its breath weapons and other limited-use abilities recover (not its spells); area, aura and ongoing damage and regeneration come once a round, at the start of its first turn (all automatic). An effect that would kill it outright, banish or imprison it, or Exhaustion from a spell, costs it its next two turns instead (yours to run); only one of Harm and Mass Harm can affect it in a fight. Damage to 0 HP still kills it.</p>",
   "treasure": "<p>Treasure type <strong>lair H</strong> (see the Treasure tables).</p>"
  }
 },
